  partName: Bolt
  description: The Bolt is a tiny, elongated component located at the middle-center-center
    of the engine, serving as a fastening element to secure various parts together.
    Despite its small size, the bolt plays a critical role in maintaining the structural
    integrity of the engine, withstanding significant stresses and loads. Interestingly,
    the bolt's material is carefully selected to provide high strength, corrosion
    resistance, and durability, ensuring reliable performance under extreme conditions.
